  "notes": "The producer behind `ugk`, authored as the writing rather than the record — which is where the two models differ. UGK's entry is the drum grammar and the ensemble; this one is the harmony and the voice. He \"learned to play many instruments by ear, including piano, trumpet, drums and flugelhorn\" and came up \"singing Italian sonnets, Negro spirituals\", and the research names gospel **plagal** cadences specifically, so the progression families here are iv-first — iv–i tags and i–iv–V blues motion — with ninths at the top of the extension weight, where the parent genre is 92% bare triads. He sings the hooks himself \"in a high, unstable register\", which is the melody block: the highest register in this batch, `structure: call_response` for the two contrasting voices the arrangement row describes, and the highest `halfStepDissonance` of any entry here, because unstable is a pitch parameter and not a description of the singer. The drum practice is his documented one — the TR-808 in place of standard drum sounds, hi-hats supplementing cymbals as an extra rhythmic tier over the 808 — so `hihat.continuous` is true, which is the opposite of the parent. The 808 keeps `role: bassline`: the research's first claim is a tuned sub with long decay carrying the tonic, and the live bass is named only as an addition on soul-based tracks, so no second bass part is grown. ⚠ The 88–96 straight funk band is NOT modelled — this entry commits to the 68–82 half-time centre, stored as its 136–164 straight equivalent, because one model spanning both feels sounds like neither. The research marks those numbers LOW-CONF; the instrument background, drum-machine practice and harmonic palette are directly sourced. ⚠ `fills.snareRollLadder` is off — with both fill periods at 4 bars the big fill wins and the inherited climbing ladder reads no seed, writing one identical fill on every one of 200. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
